{"text": "Summary:\n\nObjective:\n\nDr. Branville G. Bard, Jr.\n\nI am a dedicated, law enforcement professional with a reputation for sound leadership,\ncommunity service, fairness and innovation. Currently having over twenty-three years in\nlaw enforcement, I serve as the Chief of Police and Director of Public Safety for the\nPhiladelphia Housing Authority\u2019s Police Department PHAPD). Prior to that I served over\n21 years with the Philadelphia Police Department, more than 12 of which were at or above\nthe rank of Captain, before retiring at the rank of Inspector (Lt. Colonel). In addition to\nserving as the Chief of Police & Director of Public Safety for PHA, I was appointed by\nMayor Jim Kenney as the Co-Chair of the Public Safety Committee, for his Transition\nTeam; in this role, I was purposed with leading a group of experts in various disciplines\nwithin the field of public safety with shaping policy that ensures objectivity, community\ninvolvement, diversity and excellence.\n\nTo obtain an appointment as the head of a large to mid-size law enforcement agency that\nallows me to leverage my immense talents in the furtherance of sound governance and\ncreating true reform in policing & the Criminal Justice System.\n\nPhilosophy:\n\nEducation:\n\nIt is my firm belief that police have two overarching responsibilities: the duty owed to\nsociety to reduce crime and the fear of crime; as well as, the duty to protect the individual\nconstitutional rights\u2019 of the citizenry it is sworn to serve. I believe it is a myth that to be\nsafer as a community, we must sacrifice civil liberties; a system centered on \u201cFundamental\nFairness\u201d and \u201cSocial Justice\u201d is key.\n\nDoctorate, Public Administration (DPA)\u2014Valdosta State University\nMaster of Science, Criminal Justice (\u00a9MS)\u2014Valdosta State University\nMaster of Science, Public Safety Management (MS)}\u2014Saint Joseph\u2019s University\nEmerging Leaders, Kennedy School of Government (PGC)}\u2014Harvard University*\nFBI National Academy #227, Certificate, Criminal Justice\u2014University of Virginia\nSenior Management Institute of Policing\u2014(Police Executive Research Forum)\nBachelor of Arts, Criminal Justice (BA)\u2014Alvernia College\nAssociate of Applied Science, Justice (AAS}\u2014-Community College of Philadelphia\nDrug Unit Commander\u2019s Academy\u2014Drug Enforcement Administration\nPhiladelphia Police Academy\u2014Municipal Police Officer Certification (MPOETC, PA)\n\nProfessional Experience:\nPublic Safety:\n\n[2015-2016]\n\nCO-CHAIR PUBLIC SAFETY COMMITTEE, TRANSITION TEAM: MAYOR\nJIM KENNEY\nPurposed with leading a group of experts in various disciplines within the field of public\nsafety with shaping policy that ensures objectivity, community involvement, diversity and\nexcellence in the Administration\u2019s policies and personnel. Responsible for completed staff\nwork in the form of The Public Safety Final Transition Report.\n\n[2015-Present] PHILADELPHIA HOUSING AUTHORITY POLICE DEPARTMENT\n\nChief of Police & Director of Public Safety",
